Description: avfilter/tonemapx: reshape with MMR from the base-layer values
 A Dolby Vision MMR piece maps a component from the base-layer values
 of all three components: a constant plus coefficients on I, P, T and
 their products. tonemapx reshaped I, then P, then T, and wrote each
 result back into the values it passed to the next MMR. So the MMR of P
 read the reshaped I, and the MMR of T read the reshaped I and P. The
 C, SSE4.2, AVX2 and NEON routines all did. libplacebo and this tree's
 tonemap_cuda feed MMR the base-layer values.
 .
 The error depends on how far the luma curve moves I and on how
 strongly the chroma MMR couples to I and P. On flat synthetic profile 5
 patches whose P and T carry one first-order MMR piece each, converted
 to BT.2020 PQ, luma was up to 9 codes and chroma up to 7 codes off, and
 2.8 % of the colours were more than one luma code off.
 .
 Pass the base-layer values to every MMR. Reshaping that uses only
 polynomials does not change.
